{
  "id": "T9_primary_tests",
  "title": "Primary hypotheses (Holm-adjusted)",
  "population": "BASE paired with FINAL[v]; FINAL[v1] vs FINAL[v2] (composite)",
  "unit": "base cell",
  "notes": [
    "Composite cohort (pilot + full_ext); R04 net_gain (3 variants) and R05 variant_difference (3 pairs) for the endpoints Q06 and E02 on the composite cohort: 12 hypotheses H0: difference = 0",
    "Every hypothesis rests on the methodology's primary replicate count (B = 10,000 drawn, checked; resamples skipped for a zero denominator, if any, are counted in the CI note); everything outside this table is descriptive (unadjusted CIs, no tests); the per-block estimates of the same hypotheses are in T9b.",
    "Resolution (B = 10,000 replicates; a p below its resolution is shown as '<resolution'): p_resolution = 2/B = 0.0002 (primary family only: the smallest positive two-sided bootstrap p-value, 2 / replicates_primary; a p_value of 0 means p < p_resolution); p_holm_resolution = 0.0024 (primary family only: the Holm-adjusted resolution, the running maximum over the Holm order of (m - rank + 1) * p_resolution; a p_holm of 0 means p_holm < p_holm_resolution).",
    "Denominator exclusions (methodology missingness rules; JSON key excluded): no unit is excluded in this table by R04 (base cell(s) outside the paired cohort); R05 (base cell(s) outside the paired cohort).",
    "BL01: Includes dense_la/00 (BL-01 tolerance convention: possible false FAIL verdicts; disclosure-bearing aggregate); sensitivity SA1 in T10.",
    "IC1: Q06 is in-sample for test_feedback and combined_feedback: their loops see the ParEval test verdict and stop when it passes (every stopped_tests_pass trajectory is a Q06 pass), so they optimise the endpoint; for static_feedback Q06 is out-of-sample (measured once in phase 2, never seen by the loop). The variants therefore differ in trigger and stop rules, not only in feedback content; test_feedback cannot regress on Q06 by construction.",
    "IC2: E02 is not an independent confirmation of Q06 gains: it counts build failures, and most E02 improvements are the same cells as the Q06 improvements; the held-out signal proper is the joint transition X06 (e.g. Q06 repaired but E02 still failing) and G01.",
    "IC5: The composite primary estimates pool the pilot (12 clusters) and full_ext (48 clusters) blocks; the per-block estimates (T9b) are descriptive, the pilot ones approximate; a composite difference need not hold in both blocks.",
    "IC6: static_feedback repair triggers are dominated by clang-tidy bugprone findings and, on MPI, by low-confidence hints (design document: no trustworthy static MPI tool exists); static_feedback results measure this frozen blocking-set configuration, not static analysis in general."
  ],
  "definitions": [
    {
      "ref": "BASE",
      "text": "BASE: the 1,980 base cells (pilot_002 396 + full_ext_001 1,584), iteration-0 artifacts (use: initial code quality)"
    },
    {
      "ref": "FINAL",
      "text": "FINAL: for variant v: per base cell the artifact of the trajectory's terminal iteration (== STEP[v][2]); for trajectories terminal at iteration 0 the final artifact IS the base artifact (use: repair outcome per strategy on the identical 1,980-cell cohort)"
    },
    {
      "ref": "R04 net_gain",
      "text": "R04 net_gain: numerator = improved - regressed; denominator = cells; unit = base cell."
    },
    {
      "ref": "R05 variant_difference",
      "text": "R05 variant_difference: numerator = sum over cells of (y_v1 - y_v2); denominator = cells; unit = base cell."
    }
  ],
  "ci_note": "95% CI: nonparametric cluster bootstrap, percentile intervals, stratified by block (pilot benchmarks resampled among the 12 pilot benchmarks, full_ext among its 48); seed 20261017; cluster = benchmark; 10,000 replicates for the primary-family estimates (R04 composite with strata endpoint+variant, R05 composite with strata comparison+endpoint; Holm-adjusted tests in T9); p-values: two-sided bootstrap p = min(1, 2 * min(share of replicate differences <= 0, share >= 0)) with replicates_primary; Holm step-down at alpha 0.05 over the 12 primary hypotheses",
  "columns": [
